  "progression": [
    "The OER explicitly phases in the redesigned second and third years in 2027–2028 and 2028–2029. Current Ocasys has the new first year plus legacy and transitional higher-year entries. The eight current year-one units match Table 3 by title, semester and EC, despite code changes. The OER tables and detailed outcomes are used for subsequent years. The former BA thesis listing and one-off transition courses add no credits.",
    "Programming precedes Data Manipulation and, with Foundations of Language Technology, Machine Learning. Programming and Data Manipulation precede Search Engines. Web Development precedes Intelligent Database Design. Programming, Data Manipulation and Machine Learning precede Neural Networks and Language Models. Programming, Statistics and Machine Learning precede Information Theory. The neural course precedes Speech and Language Processing. Speech and Language Processing and Humane AI Introduction precede Ethics and Information Technology. At the thesis stage, completing the first two years meets the 120 EC threshold including all year-one courses.",
    "Year three begins with 30 EC of genuine minor space. The overlapping Data Wise and Digital Humanities minors are excluded by Article 4.2. A permitted 15 EC Information Science placement may be combined with 15 EC of minor courses. The final semester contains 5 EC ethics, 5 EC Co-Creative AI, a 10 EC Data Science Project and a distinct 10 EC thesis."
  ]
